  "structure": {
    "block_count": 34,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Colostrum 101: Learn Why Your Breasts May Leak in Pregnancy (It’s Often Very Normal!)",
        "text_sha256": "7557bc293b191add1ecbfd08e55e3462754e8952a992a9847d997fa24f6a65e1",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "pregnant woman leaking breasts",
        "text_sha256": "d516ef06e99634bda6140ed32909cafc3a7f4ab9264b32a42e90d22273abc08c",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's why your breasts leak colostrum during pregnancy and what you need to know about it.",
        "text_sha256": "558737a02cc9a4bc792956f690823f2c9e24f5ff3992e7da7e428391928ac5da",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You're aware of so many of the changes that happen to your body during pregnancy — the weight gain, the constantneed to pee, the exhaustion, the aches and pains.",
        "text_sha256": "8add8f6ef87c8a149ca187486f75c3adcc1ee1c1321d6f7828416f45f7b19690",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But there are others that happen without you even noticing, including your increased blood volume, cervical dilation , and effacement (or thinning) as your due date nears, and the production of colostrum in your breasts in preparation for baby's first meal.",
        "text_sha256": "739d57d31558479866d1351ebf14d8faa0ecbedc28b79e61618b6474af4e4e94",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Colostrum is a superfood. It's your baby's first drink! Colostrum is often called \"liquid gold\" since it's packed with nutrients and antibodies.",
        "text_sha256": "abe32c63185eed9390e4643989fb2ff406bf83fe4b3b4245f9a8dc4d17ae622c",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Leaks happen. It's normal for your breasts to drip a bit of yellow or orange liquid in the third trimester after exercise or stimulation, but not every mama will see it.",
        "text_sha256": "0343292631f5f113dc022d1ed88e582ddc5e9e9edd55f48936701dc145eb8e10",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A little is OK — but not a lot. Some leaking is expected, but if you have heavy discharge or it looks bloody, get in touch with your doc for a look-see and reassurance.",
        "text_sha256": "f27e8aa1bb37da77fcee4891505e3c6ee07f5e3b5f0dc176b898972544ff3fe6",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is colostrum?",
        "text_sha256": "831084c0e97f7d983a3b185c4a99f98c0873b5601aa05f7c36d3ccc6e282a7b2",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Colostrum, dubbed \"liquid gold\" because of its incredible antibody and nutrient content, is the precursor to the breast milk that will very soon feed your bundle of joy.",
        "text_sha256": "44a2cdd60514cd476932d742eb3abee26af537fcb5e6c3586b1b4874ac16da5f",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This yellowish, somewhat sticky fluid will be your baby's first superfood until your real milk comes in , around the third or fourth day postpartum.",
        "text_sha256": "0aca8d821699e583c6a6c7b32cd9dc0f413694f35867184fb7c182593a195fe3",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Until then, your baby will need just a few teaspoons of the antibody-rich colostrum per feeding for all her nourishment. And though it'll seem like only a little colostrum is there, your breasts will be producing more than your little one will need to fill that tiny tummy.",
        "text_sha256": "9dc3c0d438de1fb4c40a272b73d9103cb605fccac0d0480fa04279cda70db0c7",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Wondering about other pregnancy symptoms? Check out the What to Expect app for expert info about leaks, drips, spotting, and other discharge.",
        "text_sha256": "122bd796621a1de2a6a6f1af0e95b11e37cb9fd659a65e0c28b93ecc765c8d45",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Weirdest Pregnancy Symptoms",
        "text_sha256": "ddcefee9f5deb2f03bfeb8efd12ed8feff6be8b8ba071bf0a8be1dc92c9b5633",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When do pregnant women start leaking breast milk?",
        "text_sha256": "1b75816710b02c1821cf77dd4918f0e2e2df88002bd3b7f0b6034e26d0947278",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your body starts to produce colostrum in the first trimester, but moms-to-be usually don't start leaking breast milk until closer to the end of pregnancy, if it happens at all.",
        "text_sha256": "15c3f2413565b5976ffd19197fe03f6b22983839e3698a7ec31303e601265acb",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "What to Expect Community parent wessey2023 experienced leaks during one pregnancy, but not the other (go figure!). “During my first pregnancy I leaked every night starting at 24 weeks. I'm 29 weeks this time around and nothing!”",
        "text_sha256": "0cb5c06d9e5cbf9eaa6c9c277d3ec9a967755ad06173225669827b2cce4f9a24",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Why are your breasts leaking during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "b23ec6e5d33083b5870830d57bbb0c05942b2f4bd05c53437fb41be9f0f08103",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your breasts are leaking during pregnancy because prolactin, the hormone responsible for milk production after the birth of your baby , starts revving up while you're still pregnant, usually in the third trimester.",
        "text_sha256": "229d2250b2b3690bb46579598b760e739c0d579dbcc146bf32aead7b42286e84",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In fact, your hormones are performing a delicate dance during pregnancy, working hard to stay in just the right balance so that everything — from when you go into labor to when milk production starts — happens at the right time.",
        "text_sha256": "0fe69fcafd781015ba7680499147914143bc4774795a3086d14f923b5f66bc45",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The reason breast milk isn't produced in high quantities when you're expecting, especially earlier on in pregnancy, is because of the sky-high estrogen and progesterone levels that keep the milk-making in check.",
        "text_sha256": "56616d642cef51b1944d4ad7c5a0047648b66649e02d7e25b349152fb69dacb7",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If prolactin levels slightly outpace those of the estrogen and progesterone, colostrum can leak out a bit. It's normal and nothing to worry about.",
        "text_sha256": "86791a2be7544366c6b2c69b35dc299762c4750a4844f10d939258b998cbb9ab",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Also normal is to leak a little colostrum when your nipples rub against your bra during exercise, or when they're stimulated in any way — such as during sex.",
        "text_sha256": "67cd9dabe2d14ecd036a88ad7f5dd81f1b348fca5a860d7dfe6071e0e0ddf0d7",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How can you tell if you have colostrum?",
        "text_sha256": "c6363936e8ab1f5552ce0e3cdc4a400498a4cfc9e6de075de64808a86fbd5ba8",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Check the inside of your bra — do you see any small yellow or orange stains? That's a sign you're making (and leaking) a little colostrum already.",
        "text_sha256": "3114eef4860dc43d68aa7dcdfbabad638ca39d21eb13d751da6024427e88c7bc",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Not noticing that telltale sign? No worries — you can try to express a few drops by gently squeezing your areola.",
        "text_sha256": "e2538c96290fec7016629e0b14d1b6a6abc955f7877460093239b8a23ccaa8fb",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Still nothing? That's also nothing to worry about. Your breasts will get into the milk-making business when the time is right and your baby has arrived.",
        "text_sha256": "661b54de0eef0faa1837194f0d00efdfbf70c68dfb83713620ea23a80fe50104",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What can you do about colostrum and leaking breast milk during pregnancy?",
        "text_sha256": "34e1c242c4e3972a6a1eca1181e543d6b3258d8c1c78f5636e6e72638f5a448f",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're leaking colostrum, it's probably not more than a few drops. If the flow is more than you're comfortable with, wear nursing pads inside your bra to catch the extra.",
        "text_sha256": "7d2a411ea238a23ca7eadcb3d9dc701e3b813457d6cd648e2f979aac81bea5dd",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "When to call the doctor",
        "text_sha256": "ff3435591909fdafdceb4713bef36806db5b40f76c40294b17508b3f210e476c",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It's a good idea to call the doctor if you notice a lot of leakage (more than a few drops), if the colostrum is bloody, or if you have abnormal nipple discharge.",
        "text_sha256": "3d35ceb686e993b47ed9e388182d7d2ec8221820c4ae7c0d534645f700af9b9d",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Most of the time, leaking breast milk during pregnancy is nothing to be concerned about. It's just a sign that your body is gearing up for the birth of your baby!",
        "text_sha256": "91466e60d73987608086a9d94c26dcf879741b4690599f404f18b7a6a71a5413",
        "word_count": 31
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 762,
    "heading_count": 8
  },
  "title": "Colostrum: Why Are Your Breasts Leaking?",
